.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd September 6, 2026
.Dt SYS-INIT-CHECKS 1
.Os sys-init experimental
.Sh NAME
.Nm sys-init-checks
.Nd run offline development checks from a sys-init checkout
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm python3 scripts/check-all.py
.Op Fl Fl output-root Ar directory
.Nm python3 scripts/check-all.py
.Fl Fl help
.Nm python3 scripts/check-all.py
.Fl Fl version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
This manual describes the Python command in the source checkout.
There is no installed executable named
.Nm .
Run from the repository root with POSIX Python 3.10 or newer and the
separately provisioned Rust 1.98.0 toolchain.
The static gate also requires rustfmt and Clippy whose executable identities
match docs/static-tools.json on a reviewed host.
The currently pinned static-tool host is macOS arm64.
A missing or unsupported required tool cannot count as a passing check.
.Pp
The command creates a private run directory and runs ten required gates:
standards, experience, distribution, quality-process, static,
native-evidence, evidence, sample-receipts, model and host.
Each gate has a 60-second watchdog.
The first failing gate stops subsequent gates.
The report records command arguments, logs, platform and source hashes.
Source drift during the run prevents a passing result.
.Pp
These are trusted development fixtures, including real host child processes.
They do not execute a native Aether guest or establish production readiness.
Historical native evidence is checked offline; it does not replace a fresh
consuming target witness for native behavior changes.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl Fl output-root Ar directory
Parent for a new private run directory named run-*.
The default is out/checks under the repository root.
Missing parent directories are created.
Existing runs are not reused or deleted.
Choose a writable development directory; no root privileges are required.
.It Fl Fl help
Print usage and exit without running checks.
.It Fl Fl version
Print the development-check command version and exit.
This version does not identify a published sys-init release.
.El
.Pp
The exact worker invocations --evidence-worker and --sample-receipts-worker
are internal harness entry points, not ordinary check modes.
.Sh OUTPUT
Standard error contains gate progress and child diagnostics in retained logs.
Standard output contains a JSON summary with schema
sys-init-development-checks-v1, result and the absolute results.json path.
Inspect that report and adjacent stdout/stderr files after failure.
An absent, incomplete or running report is not a passing result.
Abrupt termination or filesystem failure can prevent the final summary.
Each gate has a combined 4 MiB stdout/stderr capture limit and a 60-second
deadline, including pipe draining and process exit.
The two raw logs retain their accepted prefixes in per-stream order;
ordering between streams is unspecified.
A gate record adds output_limit_bytes and reports output-limit when excess
bytes are observed, even if the child would otherwise exit zero.
The aggregate stops and exits 1 for this result.
This limit excludes child-created artifacts, source hashing and other files.
On capture failure the runner sends SIGINT to its owned group and allows up
to one additional second for the direct child to exit.
Responsive Python wrappers can unwind and clean workers in separate groups.
The runner then force-kills the remaining owned group and reaps the direct
child.
Gate records add cleanup_grace_seconds; the original failure outcome remains.
Output during the grace is not newly drained, so pipe pressure can force
fallback.
Unresponsive detached groups, abrupt aggregate termination and deeper wrappers
that kill intermediate owners remain outside this cleanup guarantee.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
The runner inherits its environment and resolves tools through PATH and rustup.
Provision tools before offline execution; the command does not install them.
Child gates receive PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1.
Do not put credentials or secrets in fixture inputs or collected logs.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa out/checks/run-*/results.json
Aggregate results, commands, source identities and not-run gates.
.It Pa out/checks/run-*/*.stdout
Per-gate standard output.
.It Pa out/checks/run-*/*.stderr
Per-gate standard error.
.It Pa docs/static-tools.json
Reviewed host formatter/linter identities and options.
.It Pa docs/*.lock
Offline shared-standard pins.
.El
.Pp
Some gates also create private artifacts under other out subdirectories.
The output-root option relocates the aggregate report, not every child artifact.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
All required gates passed and checked source identities remained unchanged;
also used for help and version.
.It 1
A required check failed, timed out, was incomplete or detected source drift.
An unhandled infrastructure exception may also exit nonzero without a summary.
.It 2
The aggregate command was invoked on a non-POSIX host.
A child static-tool block becomes an aggregate failure, not this status.
.It 64
Invalid command-line usage.
.It 130
A recorded gate invocation was interrupted.
During main-thread gate capture, SIGTERM follows the interrupted path.
The temporary handler is restored after capture; secondary SIGTERM during
cleanup is ignored.
The startup/Popen window, between-gate work, SIGKILL and repeated SIGINT
remain outside this guarantee.
Background-thread calls do not install process-global signal handlers.
Other abrupt termination is not guaranteed to produce a final report.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
From the sys-init repository root, with tools already provisioned:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
python3 scripts/check-all.py --help
python3 scripts/check-all.py
.Ed
.Pp
The first command exits zero and prints usage.
A successful second command prints ten passing gate results on standard error,
then a JSON summary on standard output, and exits zero.
On failure, retain the reported directory and diagnose the first failed gate
before retrying; a retry does not erase earlier evidence.
.Pp
Render this source manual offline from the same working directory:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
mandoc -T ascii docs/man/sys-init-checks.1
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Nm python3
and
.Nm mandoc
are host tools; their local manual availability depends on host packaging.
.Pp
Repository guides: docs/DEVELOPMENT-CHECKS.md, docs/STATIC-CHECKS.md,
docs/QUALITY-PROCESS.md and SECURITY.md.
.Sh CAVEATS
This is a source-checkout manual, not an installed-target lookup claim.
Hosted CI, other current tool hosts, native guest execution, independent
reader review and publication authorization remain separate obligations.
.Pp
Decision 0143 bounds source snapshots to 200,000 traversed entries, 10,000
selected files, 4 MiB per file and 64 MiB total, using 64 KiB digest reads.
Symlink and special entries under scanned roots reject; archive directories
remain excluded.
Read identity and final selected membership are checked sequentially.
These checks provide neither atomic snapshots nor blocking filesystem
deadlines.
.Pp
Decision 0144 publishes reports by same-directory atomic replacement.
Snapshot and expected I/O failures retain completed checks, omitted gates and
bounded stage/type/message error details; initial snapshot failure has no
hashes.
Interruption returns 130; other failures return 1.
If final publication fails, stderr receives an escaped error and no result
summary
is emitted; the last complete report may remain running.
Atomic replacement does not promise power-loss durability.
.Pp
Decision 0145 reports output-directory startup failures without inventing a
report path.
Startup interruption returns 130; other errors return 1.
Summary output is flushed; a broken summary pipe returns failure while keeping
the saved check result.
Broken progress output stops later gates and records the completed gate.
Diagnostics are best effort when stderr is unavailable.
